      "content": "\"intellectually bankrupt\" is quite a harsh judgment to make in an academic context. \n\nif we are talking about theology, isn't the very purpose of religious frameworks to provide a way of understanding reality that *extends beyond* empirical observation? if every theological claim had to be a direct mirror of current neurobiological data to be considered \"valid,\" then theology would cease to exist as a distinct field of inquiry and simply become a subset of biology.\n\nare you suggesting that for a religious tradition to remain academically or intellectually relevant, it must essentially surrender its metaphysical autonomy to the current scientific consensus?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
